 "notes": "Fig.1 (Plots/Limits_18p6.pdf), lower boundary of the solid blue 'ALP SN1987A (excl. 95%)' filled region, extracted from vector drawing (blue stroke, RGB 0.255,0.412,0.882). This is the paper's headline new limit: SN1987A axion production (Primakoff + nucleon bremsstrahlung + pion conversion, loop-induced hadronic couplings for the ALP model) followed by axion-photon conversion in the Galactic field (dominates m_a<~1e-9 eV) and the progenitor stellar magnetic field (100 G BSG, conservative; dominates above ~1e-9 eV). Excluded region is above the curve up to a validity ceiling |g|<~1e-8 GeV^-1. Low-mass floor ~2.4e-12 GeV^-1 matches the text value |g_agg|<2.6e-12 GeV^-1; shelf ~1.6e-11 GeV^-1 over ~1e-8 to ~1e-5 eV; rises for higher masses. Axis calibration from tick labels (x: 1e-12..1e-1 eV, y: 1e-16..1e-8 GeV^-1). The alternative KSVZ-like axion SN1987A hatched region (drawing 391, floor ~6e-13) was NOT chosen since the ALP model is the solid/filled headline curve. Not a dark-matter search (SN1987A), so dm_density is null.",
